      "textEn": "26\n\nIn essence, Srila Sridhar Swami praises—\n\nThe world's cycle of suffering, scattered, afflicted by various kinds of suffering. I have surrendered to you, O Lord Srinhara, to uplift me from this world. “Hey Narhari! Please, redeem those beings who have endured various kinds of suffering and\nhave been torn apart by the sharp edge of the wheel of the world, but who have somehow now found you\nand are dedicating themselves to your refuge.Victorious, with the wind blowing, the elephant, the horse,\nThey who strive, they who are very fond of gambling.\nThose who are addicted to intoxicants, their feet are held by the Guru's feet.\nLike a merchant, they are the ears of the ocean of water. 33). Meaning of the word\n\nVictorious—conquered; Hrishik—from the senses; Vayubhih—and from the life force; Adant—inexhaustible; Manah—like the mind; Tur-gam—to the horse;\nYe—who; Iha—in this world; Yatanti—they try; Yantum—to make regular; Ati—extremely; Lolam—moving;\nUpay—from the means; Khidah—being tormented; Vyasan—disaster; Shat—hundreds; Anvitah—being combined; Samavahaya—renouncing;\nGurouh—of the Guru; Charanam—to the feet; Vyanjah—merchants; Iva—like; Aja—one who is unborn; Santi—are; Akritah—not accepting;\nKaranadharaah—the oars; Jaladhaau—in the sea; Sangat—being joined; Sangat—being joined; Sangat—being joined; Sangat—being The mind is like a wild horse, which even a person who has controlled his senses and breath cannot tame. In this world, those people who want to control their minds,\nbut abandon the feet of their guru, they have to face hundreds of obstacles in the practice of various painful methods.\nHey unborn God, they are like a boat in the sea,\nSitting on it, they are like those merchants who do not hire any sailor. Meaning: To become worthy of receiving God's love, which is the ripe fruit of liberation,\nfirst, the rebellious material mind must be brought under control. Although it is difficult to do so, but when\na person, by removing